.Dd November 11, 2026
.Dt MBIND 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mbind ,
.Nm set_mempolicy_home_node
.Nd set the memory policy of a range of addresses, on a machine of one memory node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In numaif.h
.Ft long
.Fn mbind "void *addr" "unsigned long len" "int mode" "const unsigned long *nodemask" "unsigned long maxnode" "unsigned int flags"
.Ft long
.Fn set_mempolicy_home_node "unsigned long start" "unsigned long len" "unsigned long home_node" "unsigned long flags"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn mbind
gives the mappings of
.Fa len
bytes at
.Fa addr ,
rounded up to whole pages, the policy that
.Fa mode ,
.Fa nodemask
and
.Fa maxnode
describe as they do for
.Xr set_mempolicy 2 ,
and answers as Linux 6.12 answers on a machine with one memory node.
Every page is on node 0 already, so no page is placed differently; the
policy is kept and read back by
.Xr get_mempolicy 2
with
.Dv MPOL_F_ADDR ,
and
.Pa /proc/PID/numa_maps
shows it.
QEMU's memory backends, libnuma and the Java runtime call it.
.Pp
A mapping the range cuts is split at the range's ends, and neighbours left
with equal policies are joined again.
The policy stays with a mapping through
.Xr mprotect 2 ,
.Xr mremap 2
and a partial
.Xr munmap 2 ,
a child of
.Xr fork 2
has it, and
.Xr execve 2
ends it with the mappings.
For a file in memory, which is a file of tmpfs, a
.Xr memfd_create 2
file, shared anonymous memory or a System V segment, the policy belongs to
the pages of the file: every mapping of them in every process reads it, and
it lasts as long as the file.
.Dv MPOL_DEFAULT
takes the policy away.
.Pp
.Fa flags
may hold
.Dv MPOL_MF_STRICT
.Pq 1 ,
.Dv MPOL_MF_MOVE
.Pq 2
and
.Dv MPOL_MF_MOVE_ALL
.Pq 4 ,
the last for a privileged caller.
.Dv MPOL_MF_STRICT
fails with
.Er EIO ,
and sets no policy, when a page of the range is on a node the mask does
not name.
With the one node that is so only for a mask without node 0, which
.Dv MPOL_LOCAL ,
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED
with an empty mask and a mode with
.Dv MPOL_F_RELATIVE_NODES
may have, and for a page that has been written or belongs to a file: a
page that was only read is Linux's zero page, and neither it nor device
memory counts.
With a move flag such pages are moved, to node 0 where they are, and the
policy is set; a page pinned for a device cannot be moved, and
.Dv MPOL_MF_STRICT
then answers
.Er EIO
with the policy set.
.Dv MPOL_DEFAULT
ignores
.Dv MPOL_MF_STRICT .
.Pp
.Fn set_mempolicy_home_node
gives each mapping of the range that has a policy of its own the home node
.Fa home_node ,
which must be node 0.
The policy must be
.Dv MPOL_BIND
or
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED_MANY ;
a mapping without a policy is passed over.
.Xr get_mempolicy 2
does not report a home node.
.Ss System call interface
.Fn mbind
is number 274 on i386 and 237 on x86-64, and
.Fn set_mempolicy_home_node
450 on both.
On the x86-64 kernel a 32-bit program's mask is of 32-bit longs.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
0 on success.
On failure -1 is returned with
.Va errno
set; the kernel returns the negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Pa tests/numaprobe.c
binds part of a mapping, reads the policy on each side of the cut, joins
the parts again, and follows the policy through
.Xr fork 2 ,
a second mapping of shared memory and
.Dv MPOL_MF_STRICT .
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EOPNOTSUPP]"
.It Bq Er EFAULT
.Fa nodemask
cannot be read; no mapping meets the range; or, for a mode other than
.Dv MPOL_DEFAULT ,
part of the range is not mapped.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa mode ,
.Fa nodemask
or
.Fa maxnode
is one
.Xr set_mempolicy 2
refuses;
.Fa flags
has a bit other than the three;
.Fa addr
or
.Fa start
is not on a page boundary; the range wraps;
or, for
.Fn set_mempolicy_home_node ,
.Fa flags
is not 0 or
.Fa home_node
is not node 0.
.It Bq Er EIO
.Dv MPOL_MF_STRICT
found a page on a node the mask does not name, or a page a move flag
could not move.
.It Bq Er ENOENT
.Fn set_mempolicy_home_node
found no mapping with a policy of its own in the range.
.It Bq Er ENOMEM
There is no memory for the policy or for a mapping to be split.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
.Fn set_mempolicy_home_node
met a mapping whose policy is neither
.Dv MPOL_BIND
nor
.Dv MPOL_PREFERRED_MANY ;
the mappings before it have their home node.
.It Bq Er EPERM
.Dv MPOL_MF_MOVE_ALL
from a caller without privilege.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr get_mempolicy 2 ,
.Xr move_pages 2 ,
.Xr set_mempolicy 2 ,
.Xr proc 5
